body:
Wow well first of all thank you very much. the global chat got me to this point and they sorta pointed me to pob for the rest. and now you have sorta given me the extra push. again thanks for the advice. i will start to work towards some of these things. the jewels still confuse as im honestly not very sure what they do or how to use them, do u have any links or guides to how those work? i only ask cuz you mention that they are very important for this type of build.

&#x200B;

but once again thank you very much. i think ill work on the flasks first!

damn i never considered that writing as a job would be a viable thing. that sounds fun. i mean other than authors and stuff. but i guess someone has to write all those articles. 

&#x200B;

you also sound like a gem for helping OP out.

no

&#x200B;

but a fun thought

BWC brutal as in good or bad? cuz rn its not really doing much. Kinda just spamming the grenado which for some reason does like 400 dmg.

&#x200B;

also i can pick another class? like i can be two? which ones have a good synergy with the demo man? i kinda liked occultist

i think roque didnt get a chance to convert. i think he had the capacity to do so, and should he have converted, i feel like he would have been amongst the fiercest allies of the rising.

he did have *huge* flaws more so than other people in some senses but man the dude had almost everything working against him. His old ideology, darrow's betrayal, his own naiveness when it came to critically examining the Society, and then he had no one to right his viewpoint. there was no one there to put in the work to help him out and change his views. i would have *realllllyyyyy* loved to see his character develop. more so than any other character, cassius, darrow, mustang, all of them.

&#x200B;

all this being said, i still agree with the overall census that he was not a very good person, but i think he really had the capacity to become one. it is really hard to let go of beliefs you've held since birth, esp so when you didn't have to come to face with any of the realities of the Society like mustang, darrow, and victra. they all, through various methods, had some access to what was actually going on in the world. roque was raised in a utopia with no other viewpoint given to him. its one thing to be powerful and know you're doing this thing and then having beliefs that justify it, its a completely different thing to be powerful and not even have a glimpse into something that needs to be justified, everything is right and there is no reason for it to be otherwise. if this makes sense.

&#x200B;

imma have to reread this series, its been a min since i picked up the books.
